HORIZON SWEEP — is the null about the model or about how far ahead it looks?
==============================================================================
  The shipped model is trained and scored at +4h. Re-scoring the SAME scores
  against nearer horizons separates 'the model is weak' from '4h is too far'.
  The -BG column is the baseline at the same horizon: at short range 'glucose is
  already low' predicts a low trivially, and the model has to beat that to count.

